        "normally will not schedule tasks on the driver, except in the following two cases: " +
        "(1) the cluster is running in local mode, or (2) the tasks are lightweight, such as " +
        "global limit. The reason is that when no other tasks are scheduled on driver, the " +
        "driver will not be busy, and we could schedule the lightweight tasks there so that " +
        "they are likely to run faster.")
      .booleanConf
      .createWithDefault(false)

