  val UNITY_CATALOG_CLIENT_RECONCILE_COLUMN_COMMENTS =
    buildConf("spark.databricks.unityCatalog.sc178335.ucClientReconcileColumnComments.enabled")
      .doc("Mitigation flag for SC-178335, by default enabled. When it is disabled, the UC " +
        "client in DBR only parses the column comments embedded in the type json field. When it " +
        "is enabled, UC client also reads the standalone comment field in UC ColumnInfo and it " +
        "takes precedence over the type json field. " +
        "In the case when all column comment updates are issued through DBR, there is no need " +
        "to read the standalone comment field, since DBR updates and writes both fields into UC. " +
        "This change is to mitigate the issue that some caller (e.g. UI) updates the column " +
        "comment directly in UC without going through DBR, and the updates are not reflected in " +
        "DBR. What's worse is then with an update table call in UC, DBR will overwrite and wipe " +
        "out the comments added by those callers. Refer to SC-178335 for details.")
      .owner("eng-oss-spark")
      .internal()
      .booleanConf
      .createWithDefault(true)

